ls before the transport retries once.\npackages/client/src/client/auth.ts:61: * const authProvider: AuthProvider = { token: async () => process.env.API_KEY };\npackages/client/src/client/auth.ts:75:     * Called when the server responds with 401. If provided, the transport will\npackages/client/src/client/auth.ts:76:     * await this, then retry the request once. If the retry also gets 401, or if\npackages/client/src/client/auth.ts:77:     * this method is not provided, the transport throws {@linkcode UnauthorizedError}.\npackages/client/src/client/auth.ts:79:     * Implementations should refresh tokens, re-authenticate, etc. — whatever is\npackages/client/src/client/auth.ts:82:    onUnauthorized?(ctx: UnauthorizedContext): Promise<void>;\npackages/client/src/client/auth.ts:87: * Transports use this at construction time to classify the `authProvider` option.\npackages/client/src/client/auth.ts:99: * Standard `onUnauthorized` behavior for OAuth providers: extracts\npackages/client/src/client/auth.ts:100: * `WWW-Authenticate` parameters from the 401 response and runs {@linkcode auth}.\npackages/client/src/client/auth.ts:103:export async function handleOAuthUnauthorized(provider: OAuthClientProvider, ctx: UnauthorizedContext): Promise<void> {\npackages/client/src/client/auth.ts:112:        throw new UnauthorizedError();\npackages/client/src/client/auth.ts:119: * the adapted provider for `_commonHeaders()` and 401 handling, while keeping the\npackages/client/src/client/auth.ts:128:        onUnauthorized: async ctx => handleOAuthUnauthorized(provider, ctx)\npackages/client/src/client/auth.ts:139: * Transports accept `OAuthClientProvider` directly via the `authProvider` option —\npackages/client/src/client/auth.ts:216:     * are included in token exchange and refresh requests. When provided, this method\npackages/client/src/client/auth.ts:373:export class UnauthorizedError extends Error {\npackages/client/src/client/auth.ts:375:        super(message ?? 'Unauthorized');\np